  "title": "School profile"
 },
 "description": "The full SchoolScope profile for one school by slug: verdict and archetype, Scope Score with band and percentile per level, CAASPP exceeded/met split, cohort growth (school-by-grade aggregates two years apart, in SBAC scale-score points, reported as a 0-100 index centred on the state average), climate (absenteeism, suspension, ELPAC), equity gaps by student group, teacher stability, and \u2014 for high schools \u2014 graduation, college destinations, UC admissions history, AP courses, and IB programmes. Also answers \"is this school improving?\" with a year-over-year table of statewide percentile and the underlying rates; the Scope Score is excluded there because it is normalised within each year and is not comparable across them. For public schools it also returns the profile's own `answer` (one sentence about all students, each subject against California's rate for the same grades), up to three selected `takeaways` (each with figures, comparisons, a question where one applies, and a generated receipt naming source, year, grades, population, n and how the comparison was built), and `studentGroups` (every group by income, race or ethnicity, language and disability with 30+ students tested in each subject, against the same group in the same grades in the district and statewide). Current data year 2025.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
